":"pdf"},{"id":"p1-c13","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":35,"text":"Tier II 15005 18538 18850\nTotal (Tier I+II) 126695 146470 151698\nRisk-weighted Assets 782134 852991 882732\nGross Advances 1151041 1293381 1375060\n12.21 12.91 12.80\nRWA to Gross Advances (%) 67.95 65.95 64.20\nTier I (%) 14.28 15.00 15.05\nCommon Equity Tier I (%) 12.21 12.91 12.80\nAdditional Tier I (%) 2.07 2.09 2.25\nSep'25 Jun'26 Sep'26\nCET AT I TIER II\nTier II (%) 1.92 2.17 2.14\nTotal (Tier I+II) % 16.20 17.17 17.19 Confidential\nPage 34\nShareholding Pattern as on September 30th, 2026\nYear ended FII/FPIs holding (%)\nMar’25 10.55\nStaff, 0.57 Others, 2.40\nResident Individuals, 10.51\nMar’26 14.24\nSep’26 12.27\nFIIs/FPIs, 12.27\nMutual Funds, 7.00\nGovernment of India, 62.93 Insurance Companies, 4.32\nConfidential\nPage 35\nA Legacy of Trust Togetherness Transformation\nEnvironmental, Social & Governance\nConfidential\nPage 36\nEnvironmental, Social & Governance (ESG) Practices\nEnvironmental Social Governance\n As part of Green initiatives, Bank has undertaken:  Increased usage of LED light, BEE rated AC units","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Oct 2026","document_date":"2026-10-15","document_rank":1,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p1-c14","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":38,"text":" As part of Green initiatives, Bank has undertaken:  Increased usage of LED light, BEE rated AC units\n Bank is impacting the Society by engaging in helping and uplifting underserved communities through non profit organizations viz  Canara Centenary Rural Development Trust  Canara Financial Advisory Trust  Canara Golden Jubilee Education Fund  Canara Relief and Welfare Society  Financial Literacy Centers (FLC)  Rural Self Employment Training Institutes (RSETIs)  Rural Development & Self Employment Training Institutes ( RUDSETIs.)  During September 2026 quarter, Bank has conducted 1260 awareness programs and 729 training programs through its RSETIs and RUDSETIs, benefiting 20,000 plus candidates to upgrade their skill sets.  Bank has 150 Financial Literacy Centers (FLCs) through which 7,550 camps have been conducted and 7,91,056 persons were extended Financial Literacy during September 2026 quarter.  To promote diversity , equity & inclusive growth, Bank has in place a Women Empowerment Committee named as ‘Advaita’ to support the women employee fraternity of the Bank.","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Oct 2026","document_date":"2026-10-15","document_rank":1,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p1-c15","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":38,"text":" For the Bank’s journey towards Sustainability, Bank has in place:  Board approved ESG Policy.  Green Deposit Policy & Lending Framework.  The Bank publishes its BRSR annually as part of the Annual Report, along with a dedicated Sustainability Report that highlights its initiatives in environmental stewardship, social empowerment, and long-term resilience.  Bank has a Chief Ethics Officer and an exclusive ‘Ethics Section’ is in place to oversee the implementation of business ethics in the organization.  Bank has been recognized for “Excellent Practices and Adoption of ESG Initiatives” at the 2nd ICC Emerging Asia Conclave 2024, organized by the Indian Chamber of Commerce.  Bank’s ESG Risk Rating has been improved from High to Medium by Sustainalytics, reflecting its enhanced sustainability performance.\n Gradual phasing out of DG sets\n Installed Rain Water Harvesting system in all 122 feasible Bank owned properties and Solar Rooftop Power system across 174 Bank owned properties, with a total capacity of 4417 kWp.\n EV charging station has been commissioned in Head Office Building for charging of staff’s E-Vehicles.","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Oct 2026","document_date":"2026-10-15","document_rank":1,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p1-c16","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":38,"text":" EV charging station has been commissioned in Head Office Building for charging of staff’s E-Vehicles.\n Bank has been awarded a total of 44 Green building certifications, including 42 office premises and one training center (Canara Institute of Bank Management-Manipal) accredited under the IGBC Green Building certification framework, of which 7 buildings have been accorded Silver rating. Further, Bank’s 1 Residential building has been certified under GRIHA (Green Rating for Integrated Habitat).\n Bank is having a significant portfolio under sustainable finance which includes Renewable Energy Projects, Compressed Biogas & Energy Conservation scheme, Solar Pump scheme under PM-KUSUM, Roof Top Solar (RTS) for residential sector with subsidy, Canara Green Wheels scheme for E vehicles.\n Scope 1 & Scope 2 emissions of the bank accounts for a total of 11272.51 tCO2 and 165168.84 tCO2 respectively for the financial year 2025-26.\nConfidential\nPage 37\nA Legacy of Trust Togetherness Transformation\nLondon, UK\n10100+ Branches Across India\nNew York, USA Dubai (DIFC), UAE\nIBU Gift City, Gujarat 24/7\nCustomer Support\nDistribution Network\nConfidential\nPage 38\nDistribution Network\nParameters Sep’25 Jun’26 Sep’26\nGeneral Branches(a) 9321 9497 9512\nSpecialised Branches(b) 627 634 634\nTotal Domestic Branches(a+b) 9948 10131 10146\nOverseas Branches 4 4 4\nBC Points 11076 12490 13087","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Oct 2026","document_date":"2026-10-15","document_rank":1,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p1-c17","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":40,"text":"BC Points 11076 12490 13087\nTotal Banking Outlets 21028 22625 23237\nTotal ATM & Recycler 10866 11047 10764\nPresence across Urban & Rural areas Sep’26\n4 International Branches\nUrban\nRural\n1994 19% Metro\n3215 32%\n• New York • London • DIFC Dubai • IBU Gift City Branch\n1897 19% Semi-Urban\n3040 30%\nConfidential\nPage 39\nA Legacy of\nTrust Togetherness Transformation\nDigi